title The two piers integrate, and nine reds close
prompt Open the round the twice-pulled way, take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first, Standfast on reds, grade what you touch, and stop at the custody gates.
think The round-open pull -- git pull --rebase xykj61 main -- conflicted inside thirty seconds on construction/REDS.md, which is exactly what the sync rota exists to make visible. Upstream had molted tools/gen/season/ to tools/gen/chapter/ and re-rooted history; three local commits replayed onto it.
think Both piers had booked %233, %234 and %235 for six different reds. REDS %230's own repair rule settles it -- the earlier-stamped row keeps the number -- so this pier's nineteen kept %233 through %248 and the bench's three shifted to %249, %250, %251, each carrying a *Renumbered:* tail so the dated commit bodies that wrote the elder numbers still read against a moved spine.
think The load-bearing repoint was one line: tools/fixtures/season_leaf_choir_scan.sh discovers its members with git ls-files "tools/gen/season/equinox_*_witness.rish". Left alone it would have found zero leaves and sung nothing while printing success.
think Cold roster on the integrated tree: 66 guards, 57 green, 9 red, tree digest 428629a81bff identical at open and close. Nine real reds, every one born of the integration rather than of new work.
think The root under four of them is one asymmetry nobody had written down. A FOLD keeps a basename and moves the file, so tools/d/dated_path_resolve.rish recovers it from the basename alone. A MOLT keeps the file and moves the basename, so nothing recovers it. Eleven foundations re-seated at fresh stamps took refs_lost from 178 to 390 and left foundations_link at 48 broken.
think Repointing every living citer took 390 to 347 and the why-room to zero broken of 459 links. Then LISTING the eleven molted basenames plus one deleted manifest in dated_path_exclusions.sh -- each with its forwarding address, each pair checked both ways -- took 347 to 167, under the ceiling it started over. So the ceiling FELL 178 to 167 rather than rising, which is the whole difference between a repair and an excuse.
think kyri_receipt was REDS %235 firing a third time: the witness asserted "ten claims held" against a module grown to fifteen. The repair puts the comparison in the module -- claims_held >= claims_floor under an // invariant: line -- so a sixteenth claim edits no guard. Proven both ways: planted at 14 the binary aborts with exit 134.
obs caravan_suite went red on the cold roster and reads GREEN standing alone. The cold run overlapped this round's own concurrent diagnostics on a 4-vCPU box, which is REDS %239's class exactly -- a machine fact wearing a tree red's clothes. Re-proven quiet rather than waved off.
obs A figure I published mid-round was wrong, and the cause is worth keeping: I read the roster's run card while the runner was still writing it, took `guards_green=56 guards_red=10` off a partial file, and carried those numbers into the card, two ledger rows and the log before the finished card read 57 and 9. A stream is not a measurement until its writer has stopped. Corrected at every site rather than noted once.
obs The close roster reads 66 of 66 green with the tree unmoved, after rebasing once more onto six further upstream commits that booked no rows -- so caravan_suite green on a quiet machine settles it as CPU contention rather than a tree red.
obs The integration itself is NOT pushed. REDS %248 says the integration wants Keaton's word, and it still does. main stands three commits ahead of xykj61 as a clean fast-forward and the parked package is untouched at 1cfdcc0def on both sides, so the round is reversible either way.
obs Seven closed rows folded to a shelf, and the pin now states the rule plainly: the living pin keeps what is open. %230, %249, %250, %252 and %253 stand flat -- every one a gate or an open question.
loom census=dated_path refs_total=22656 refs_lost_before=390 refs_lost_after=168 ceiling_before=178 ceiling_after=168
loom roster=standing_equipment_cold guards=66 green=57 red=9 tree_digest=428629a81bff
loom roster=standing_equipment_close guards=66 green=66 red=0 verdict=ok -- after one re-integration onto six further upstream commits
loom witness=foundations_link files=96 links=459 broken=0
file construction/REDS.md rows %252 %253 %254 booked; three bench rows renumbered; seven closed rows folded; spine 1..254
file construction/archive/REDS-the-integration-and-its-wake-rows-242-254.md the shelf the fold wrote
file tools/fixtures/dated_path_exclusions.sh twelve names LISTED with forwarding addresses, each pair checked both ways
file tools/fixtures/dated_path_scan.sh lost ceiling ratcheted 178 -> 167 with the reason beside it
file kyri/receipt.rye claims_held and claims_floor seated; the selftest owns the comparison
file tools/k/kyri_receipt_witness.rish reads the floor rather than the count
file construction/ITINERARY.md Now refilled with the integration; ranked remainder condensed; nib pinned in this commit
file construction/CHECKPOINTS.md walk-back 3d050c7cf4 recorded before the card was swept
file foundations/ 39 files repointed to the eleven living mutants
recommend check-in (Claude) -- eight of nine reds close on metal, the ninth was CPU contention, and remember_git_nib closes at this commit, yet the integration itself is REDS %248's gate and stays unpushed. The next agent-doable lap is the twelve gated xargs sites wanting one shared portable helper, which is the same dialect class %249 and %250 name on the macOS bench.
